I'm wrong about the input.cpp snippet above which is for function void Input::joy_axis(int p_device, JoyAxis p_axis, float p_value).  This function never gets called.  Rather void Input::joy_button(int p_device, JoyButton p_button, bool p_pressed) is used.

The Joypad.last_buttons is reflecting the proper state... so I'm baffled why my gdscript doesn't report all pressed.

I guess next step is to see what happens between joy.last_buttons and Input.is_action_pressed.

```gdscript
